It this case it probably worth doing for readability, but also the whole size calculation can be moved into the same if block:

```c++
	uint64_t read  = 0;
	if (p_dst && data) {
		uint64_t left = length - pos;
		read = MIN(p_length, left);

		if (read < p_length) {
			WARN_PRINT("Reading less data than requested");
		}

		memcpy(p_dst, &data[pos], read);
		pos += read;
	}
	return read;
```

